sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch04-04> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch04-04: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.55" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.545"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.66"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "Colour match and predator survival form a clear confirming and refuting contrast, and published experiments already cover insects and a few birds. Those survival data are not gathered in a single downloadable database, and photo archives only proxy the pattern. A compilation could test a familiar subset of visually hunted prey, with serious but manageable alternative functions of colour." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: Score prey colour against the background where the animal is found, and compare attack rates on matching and mismatched forms by visually hunting predators. Higher survival of matching forms would confirm a protective effect of the tint; equal survival after accounting for temperature and sexual signalling would refute it. Open photo and specimen archives support the match, while the survival contrast lives mainly in individual experiments." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Predation trials that measure the survival benefit are scattered across papers rather than one open table.", "Background matching can serve thermoregulation or sexual display as well as crypsis.", "Photographs over-represent conspicuous and diurnal animals." ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok--dataset-3> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch04-04--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch04-04 by Grok 4.7: 0.78" ;
